  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 43. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 古城 — 昔に建てられた城。\n2. 個人差 — 人によって違うこと。\n3. コスチューム — 舞台や特定の場面などで着る衣装。\n4. コスト — 物を作ったり仕事をしたりするための費用。\n5. 子育て — 子どもが育つのを世話して支えること。\n6. 骨格 — 体を支える骨の組み立て。\n7. 小包 — 荷物を包んで送る郵便物など。\n8. コテージ — 休暇などに泊まる小さな独立した家。\n9. 孤島 — 陸地やほかの島から離れた島。\n10. 事柄 — ある具体的な出来事や内容。\n11. 言葉遣い — 場面や相手に合わせた言葉の使い方。\n12. 鼓動 — 心臓が動いてどきどきと打つこと。\n13. 小道具 — 舞台や撮影などで使う小さな道具。\n14. 粉ミルク — 乳などを粉状に加工したもの。\n15. 琥珀 — 昔の木の樹脂が長い時間をかけて固まったもの。\n16. コピー機 — 紙にある文字や絵を別の紙に写す機械。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
